From 4f3e13d118a8b11294882d5b8dae41e3d0a03adb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CyberDog Port <port@local>
Date: Sun, 19 Jul 2026 11:44:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] audio: convert rt5680 + tas5805m from 4.9 snd_soc_codec
 to 5.10 component API

Mechanical legacy-API->component-API conversion (multi-agent, cross-reviewed,
each compile-verified to a clean .o):
- snd_soc_codec_driver -> snd_soc_component_driver (flattened .component_driver
  sub-struct; added idle_bias_on/use_pmdown_time/endianness/non_legacy_dai_naming)
- snd_soc_register_codec -> devm_snd_soc_register_component
- snd_soc_read/write/update_bits/*_get_drvdata -> component equivalents
  (snd_soc_component_read returns the value directly in 5.10)
- rt5680: probe/remove/suspend/resume/set_bias_level -> component signatures
- tas5805m: .digital_mute -> .mute_stream(dai,mute,dir) + no_capture_mute
All register tables, DAPM widgets/routes, and the 1740-line tas5805m_basic.h
DSP tuning table are byte-for-byte unchanged (verified via git diff --stat).
